<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>JSql</RootNamespace>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Platforms>AnyCPU;x64</Platforms>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Label="nuget package">
    <PackageId>JSql</PackageId>
    <Version>1.0.2.123</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>1.0.2.123</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>1.0.2.123</FileVersion>
    <Title>JSql - an experimental sql engine over pluggable file storage</Title>
    <AssemblyTitle>JSql</AssemblyTitle>
    <Description>JSql is an experimental SQL engine written in VB.NET. It ships a hand written SQL front end (tokenizer, recursive descent parser and execution engine) for a MySQL compatible subset, on top of a pluggable file based storage layer. Physical storage is abstracted by IDbFileStorageProvider, so the file engine can be swapped at runtime: the built in TextFileStorage backend keeps one database as one folder (a per-table .schema.json schema file plus JSONL or CSV row data guarded by a write ahead log), while other backends such as the SQLite file backend are injected through SqlEngine.SetStorage. Supported: CREATE/DROP DATABASE, TABLE and INDEX, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, and SELECT with DISTINCT, INNER/LEFT JOIN, WHERE, GROUP BY, HAVING, ORDER BY and LIMIT, arithmetic and comparison expressions, aggregates, plus persisted column indexes (hash, range and full text) that are rebuilt after a write and restored on restart.</Description>
    <PackageTags>scibasic;jsql;sql;sql-engine;sql-parser;database;storage-engine;jsonl;csv;sqlite;wal;vbnet</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>1.0.2.123
+ IDbFileStorageProvider: the storage layer is now a pluggable, database scoped backend contract (database/table catalog, table sessions, load/save/delete, storage diagnostics).
+ SqlEngine can switch the physical file engine at runtime through SetStorage(provider) or New(provider, options); the Catalog property is kept as a backwards compatible alias.
* DatabaseCatalog is renamed to TextFileStorage and now implements IDbFileStorageProvider, the jsonl/csv on disk layout is unchanged.
* IndexManager depends on IDbFileStorageProvider instead of the concrete catalog.
+ New JSql.Sqlite backend: one JSql database is stored as one .sqlite file holding every table of that database.
+ REPL host: new --backend text|sqlite switch (alias --engine) that injects the storage provider.
Earlier: pluggable row codecs (JSONL / CSV), sparse line index plus WAL text line store, persisted column indexes.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>xieguigang &lt;I@xieguigang.me&gt;</Authors>
    <Company>sciBASIC.NET Foundation</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2021-2026 この中二病に爆焔を！</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/xieguigang/JSql</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/xieguigang/JSql</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <IncludeSymbols>True</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="True" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\GCModeller\src\runtime\Darwinism\src\data\LINQ\LINQ\LINQ.vbproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\GCModeller\src\runtime\sciBASIC#\Data\DataFrame\dataframework-netcore5.vbproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\GCModeller\src\runtime\sciBASIC#\Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core\src\Core.vbproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
